WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:14.060
The Monk trembled with fear.

2
00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:16.823
angry voice spoke again.

3
00:00:16.843 --> 00:00:19.565
"Who is walking on my mountain?"

4
00:00:19.645 --> 00:00:22.488
"Ahh!" cried the Tang Monk.

5
00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:26.152
He fell off his horse and tumbled down the mountain.

6
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.302
At the bottom he saw a crack between the rocks.

7
00:00:35.424 --> 00:00:40.949
The monk looked in and saw a moss-covered monkey peering out at him.

8
00:00:40.969 --> 00:00:44.412
"My name is Sun Wukong," said the monkey.

9
00:00:44.432 --> 00:00:47.474
"I am king of the Fruit and Flower Mountain."

10
00:00:49.296 --> 00:00:49.996
are you in there?"

11
00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:51.397
asked the Tang Monk.

12
00:00:51.998 --> 00:00:54.340
He stood up.

13
00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.241
"Buddha put me here," said Wukong.

14
00:00:57.222 --> 00:00:59.324
am being punished for causing trouble in Heaven.

15
00:01:00.236 --> 00:01:00.696
Who are you?"

16
00:01:02.077 --> 00:01:04.038
"I'm just a monk," said the Tang Monk.

17
00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:07.821
"I'm going to the Western Paradise to get scriptures from Buddha."

18
00:01:09.121 --> 00:01:10.082
Wukong gasped.

19
00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:12.183
"You're the Tang Monk!"

20
00:01:12.503 --> 00:01:13.044
he cried.

21
00:01:13.064 --> 00:01:14.945
"I'm supposed to go with you!"

22
00:01:16.786 --> 00:01:18.627
Tang Monk took a step back.

23
00:01:19.668 --> 00:01:21.969
Was this strange monkey telling the truth?

24
00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.532
"The bodhisattva Guanyin visited me," Wukong went on.

25
00:01:28.008 --> 00:01:31.269
"She said I'd be set free if I promise to protect you on the journey.

26
00:01:32.349 --> 00:01:34.490
Set me free, and I'll go with you to the West."

27
00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:36.951
Tang Monk relaxed.

28
00:01:38.291 --> 00:01:39.271
He looked at the rocks.

29
00:01:40.432 --> 00:01:41.352
"How can I free you?"

30
00:01:41.372 --> 00:01:45.693
"There's a small piece of paper on top of this mountain," said Wukong.

31
00:01:46.694 --> 00:01:47.834
"You must remove it."

32
00:01:52.635 --> 00:01:54.836
The Tang Monk went back up the mountain.

33
00:01:55.904 --> 00:02:00.468
He pushed aside shrubs and brambles and pulled himself over large boulders.

34
00:02:07.013 --> 00:02:09.335
Finally he reached the mountain's peak.

35
00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.001
monk picked up the paper.

36
00:02:18.282 --> 00:02:20.924
Right away a breeze swept it from his hand.

37
00:02:22.525 --> 00:02:25.568
The paper floated up and then disappeared among the clouds.

38
00:02:27.264 --> 00:02:29.086
The monk hurried back down the mountain.

39
00:02:29.106 --> 00:02:34.050
"The paper floated away," he said to the monkey.

40
00:02:35.831 --> 00:02:37.732
returned to Buddha," said Wukong.

41
00:02:37.752 --> 00:02:39.134
"Now step back."

42
00:02:39.994 --> 00:02:41.916
The Tang Monk took a step back.

43
00:02:41.936 --> 00:02:45.879
"Go farther," said Wukong.

44
00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.581
The monk took another step back.

45
00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:51.904
"Go farther," said Wukong again.

46
00:02:55.052 --> 00:02:57.354
The Tang Monk went far from the mountain.

47
00:02:59.055 --> 00:03:02.717
He gasped as the entire mountain rose into the air.

48
00:03:04.058 --> 00:03:07.460
Wukong stood under the mountain, holding it up with his hands.

49
00:03:09.762 --> 00:03:13.064
He jumped out, and the mountain crashed down behind him.

50
00:03:17.547 --> 00:03:19.589
Wukong grabbed the Tang Monk's hands.

51
00:03:19.609 --> 00:03:21.610
"Thank you, Master!

52
00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.092
I will help you reach the Western Paradise."

53
00:03:26.156 --> 00:03:28.898
The Tang Monk rode the horse as Wukong walked.

54
00:03:29.938 --> 00:03:31.699
The monkey told the monk about himself.

55
00:03:31.719 --> 00:03:35.381
"The Jade Emperor's entire army couldn't defeat me."

56
00:03:36.141 --> 00:03:36.722
He laughed.

57
00:03:37.262 --> 00:03:40.504
"So I said should be in charge of Heaven."

58
00:03:40.524 --> 00:03:42.805
"What powers do you have?"

59
00:03:43.285 --> 00:03:44.166
asked the Tang Monk.

60
00:03:44.186 --> 00:03:47.908
"I can become other animals," said Wukong.

61
00:03:47.928 --> 00:03:49.529
"Watch this!"

62
00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:53.651
quickly changed into a tiger.

63
00:03:54.411 --> 00:03:56.688
The Tang Monk gulped.

64
00:03:56.748 --> 00:04:01.010
Wukong changed into a snake, a vulture, and then back into himself.

65
00:04:02.231 --> 00:04:03.591
that's not all," he said.

66
00:04:03.611 --> 00:04:04.992
"I can grow big!"

67
00:04:08.413 --> 00:04:12.255
The monkey's body grew so big that his head reached the clouds.

68
00:04:12.275 --> 00:04:15.396
"And I can become tiny!"

69
00:04:15.696 --> 00:04:16.477
said Wukong.

70
00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:20.679
He shrank to the size of a bee and hopped onto the monk's head.

71
00:04:22.059 --> 00:04:22.659
can do more!"

72
00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:23.560
said Wukong.

73
00:04:25.344 --> 00:04:27.626
He changed back to his normal size.

74
00:04:28.627 --> 00:04:30.949
His iron bar appeared from his ear.

75
00:04:33.651 --> 00:04:36.874
The monkey spun it around and then struck a huge boulder.

76
00:04:39.696 --> 00:04:42.218
The boulder exploded into tiny pieces.

77
00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.941
The Tang Monk watched in horror.

78
00:04:47.923 --> 00:04:51.005
laughed. "Don't look so scared, Master.

79
00:04:51.686 --> 00:04:54.664
I'm protecting you!"

80
00:04:54.764 --> 00:04:58.447
The two traveled farther until they saw a group of men blocking the road.

81
00:05:00.089 --> 00:05:01.750
men looked rough and mean.

82
00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:03.211
They all had weapons.

83
00:05:04.913 --> 00:05:07.415
One man stepped forward and waved a sword.

84
00:05:07.435 --> 00:05:11.018
"Give us your money, or you'll be sorry!"
